      "The attack follows five stages (register app, craft lure to the real consent URL, victim consents, attacker uses the token, attacker persists via refresh token), and each stage leaves a trace, with the 'Consent to application' audit event being the pivotal one for detection.",
      "Detection reads real Entra audit log fields (activityDisplayName, initiatedBy.user.userPrincipalName, targetResources[].modifiedProperties with the granted scopes) to find unfamiliar apps granted sensitive, durable scopes; a Sentinel AuditLogs query can proactively surface existing risky grants tenant-wide.",
      "Defence is restricting user consent, enabling an admin consent workflow, and reviewing existing grants; response requires revoking the app consent and refresh tokens, not just resetting the password, since the attacker's access was never tied to the password in the first place."
