        "explanation": "Run/RunOnce are the most famous ASEPs but far from the only ones: Winlogon Userinit and Shell values (T1547.004), Policies\\Explorer\\Run, RunServices, BootExecute, IFEO Debugger values (T1546.012), COM InprocServer32 hijacks (T1546.015), and the Startup folder all auto-launch code. A clean Run key narrows nothing on its own, which is why tools like Autoruns enumerate the whole set. Options b, c, and d all falsely assert Run keys are the only autostart mechanism."
