        "answer": "a",
        "explanation": "PSEXESVC is the default, unobfuscated service name PsExec creates on a target, so seeing it does not by itself distinguish legitimate admin use from attacker lateral movement — you need surrounding context like the logon type, the account used, and whether that account's use makes sense, exactly as the worked example shows. Option b is false; 7045 does record the service name. Option c invents encryption that does not exist. Option d misdefines Logon Type 3, which is a network logon, not an interactive console logon."
